        "evidence": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_244b113541c8_0006",
            "text": "As a result, any dynamically calculated fee above 10% gets rejected reducing potential protocol revenue. Potential user discounts applied in `getFee()` are lost when the factory rejects the final fee. And the 50% anti-MEV protection cap becomes unusable, leaving pools vulnerable to maximal extractable value attacks during high volatility"
          }
